## Extending Interfaces
Interfaces can inherit from other interfaces:
```ts
interface User {
    name: string;
    email: string;
}

interface Creator extends User {
    subscribers: number;
    verified: boolean;
}
```

`Creator` has everything `User` has, plus its own properties. A `Creator` must have `name`, `email`, `subscribers`, AND `verified`.

## Reopening Interfaces
Unlike `type`, interfaces can be reopened and extended:
```ts
interface Video {
    title: string;
}

interface Video {
    views: number;
}

// Video now has BOTH title and views
const v: Video = { title: "Cat", views: 100 };
```

This is called **declaration merging**. It's how libraries add properties to existing types like `Window`.


